he's, of course, taking this time to enjoy himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:39.120
as a new parent and to spend some time with the&nbsp;
little one and get some sleep whenever he can find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:42.800
the time to. Today, we're gonna be talking about&nbsp;
a number of different topics. We're going to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:47.280
talking about the January 6th hearings. We're&nbsp;
going to talk about inflation and gas prices&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:51.680
and all these different things. But I wanted to&nbsp;
start today talking about gun control, because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:58.000
there's a new bipartisan deal in the Senate on&nbsp;
the topic of gun control, and it actually includes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.720
ten Republican senators, which is crucial because&nbsp;
that means there's a solid chance of this actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:06.960
passing in the coming weeks and becoming&nbsp;
law. I don't want to celebrate it too much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:12.080
because for one, it hasn't actually happened yet.&nbsp;
Right. And these things could fall through. We we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:17.520
need to see the actual text, but also it&nbsp;
seems a little bit lackluster. It doesn't come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.760
nearly close to all the things that we have to&nbsp;
do to actually make a difference when it comes to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:27.680
guns and gun safety in this country. But given&nbsp;
the fact that Republicans have been steadfast in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:33.120
their refusal to do anything about guns in&nbsp;
the wake of mass shootings over the years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:39.600
it's hard to not feel some level of optimism over&nbsp;
this announced agreement. The deal will include&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:45.440
support for state crisis intervention orders,&nbsp;
funding for school safety resources, an enhanced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:51.520
review process for buyers of guns under the age of&nbsp;
21, and penalties for straw purchases. That's when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:56.800
you have one person purchase a weapon on someone&nbsp;
else's behalf. The legislation will also have a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:01.600
red flag provision so that states and courts will&nbsp;
have the resources to make sure firearms are kept&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:06.720
out of the hands of people who are at significant&nbsp;
risk of doing harm with them. There's also going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:12.720
to be increased funding for mental health, suicide&nbsp;
prevention and trauma intervention, which is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:16.800
of course, an important aspect to all of this. We&nbsp;
know that the right wing in this country loves to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:21.920
claim that mass shootings are all about mental&nbsp;
health and that they're just exclusively a mental&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:26.240
health issue. We know that they just use it as&nbsp;
a red herring. But there's there's something to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:30.960
that, right? Because that is one aspect in all of&nbsp;
this. And we have to not only look at gun control&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:34.320
measures, we have to look at the mental health&nbsp;
side as well. So if they're willing to have a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:39.360
good faith conversation about mental health, we&nbsp;
should absolutely take them up on that and take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:44.720
advantage of it. The ten Republican senators who&nbsp;
have signed on to this piece of legislation that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:51.840
in the works are John Cornyn, Thom Tillis, Richard&nbsp;
Burr, Roy Blunt, Bill Cassidy, Susan Collins,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:59.280
Lindsey Graham, Rob Portman, Mitt Romney and Pat&nbsp;
Toomey. The centrist Democrats who tend to torpedo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:04.960
pieces of legislation that we like as progressives&nbsp;
and Democrats. Those are Joe Manchin and Kirsten&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:09.680
